# Project-specific rules only. Secrets, Python and OS noise are handled once at
# the repo root; these paths are relative to this file, so they scope cleanly to
# running/ and cannot reach another project's `data/`.

# ── Media and run artifacts ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# No videos live in the repo. `data/input/` is where you drop your own clip,
# `data/cache/` holds converted MP4s and cached gateway responses, and
# `data/output/` gets one timestamped directory per run. All of it is local.
#
# Ignored as a blanket rather than per subdirectory, so a clip dropped straight
# into `data/` cannot be committed either. Git does not descend into an ignored
# directory, which is why `data/input/` has to be re-admitted before its own
# contents can be excluded and `.gitkeep` let back in.
data/*
!data/input/
data/input/*
!data/input/.gitkeep
